implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review of this task's own diff; this is the final step. Load the adversarial-self-review skill first.

Attack the code on these points:
- Concurrency: replies arriving out of order; a reply arriving after its timeout; a reconnect while old ids are still pending.
- Input sizes: inputs that are empty, huge or deeply nested; a line exactly at its limit; a frame exactly at its limit.
- Prototype-style role names, such as 'constructor'.
- Any error message that could carry input text.
- Any blocking call that could stall the loop.
- Any code path that reads an environment variable other than MOE_ROLE, or opens a socket other than AF_UNIX to AGENT_SOCKET.

Then run mutation probes. Work in a scratch copy: cp -r scripts/local-runner and scripts/tests into a mktemp dir, and never mutate the shared tree. Run each probe as `timeout 120 node --test --test-name-pattern='^SH[0-9] ' <copy>/tests/local-runner-agents.test.mjs`. For the R07 probes, use the matching R07 test name against the copy's local-runner.test.mjs. Score each probe by exit code, never by parsing the pass/fail lines.

Each mutant must be killed by the named row:
- load_tools skips validation (SH1);
- the role is ignored, or a non-str role is accepted (SH1);
- the argument-key check is dropped (SH3);
- an error message is built from input (SH3);
- the line bound uses >= instead of > (SH6);
- the frame bound is dropped (SH6);
- the in-flight bound is dropped (SH6);
- deadlines never expire (SH6);
- the outbox is replaced by sendall (SH6, paused peer);
- the host length bound is dropped (SH7);
- an id never assigned is treated as a late reply (SH7);
- the CODE check on ok:false is dropped (SH7);
- the socket path comes from an environment variable (SH8);
- the shimHash check is removed (its R07 row);
- the shim is written '0755' (the R07 buildUserData row and SH9).

If a mutant survives, add a test that kills it, unless the mutant is provably equivalent; then say why in the step note. Afterwards, kill any python3 processes you started (match by your own scratch dir path) and remove the scratch dir.
